From: felias-fogg <nebel@hinterm-ziel.de>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:06:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] PICkit 5/Basic: enable the data endpoints with
 libusb-win32 (MSVC builds)

pickit5.c includes <usb.h> (HAVE_USB_H) or, in MSVC builds on Windows,
<lusb0_usb.h> (HAVE_LUSB0_USB_H), but the block with usbdev_bulk_recv(),
usbdev_bulk_send() and usbdev_check_connected() was only compiled for
HAVE_USB_H. MSVC builds got the stubs that return -1, so every transfer on
the data endpoints failed silently: signature and fuses could be read
(command endpoints), but reading or writing flash and EEPROM failed with
"reading data memory failed" / "sending script with download failed",
after which the programmer had to be reconnected.

Use the real functions whenever a libusb-0.1 API is available, as the
rest of pickit5.c already does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/pickit5.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/pickit5.c b/src/pickit5.c
index 6619c04a..afbc2cb5 100644
--- a/src/pickit5.c
+++ b/src/pickit5.c
@@ -2197,7 +2197,7 @@ void pickit5_initpgm(PROGRAMMER *pgm) {
 
 
 
-#if defined(HAVE_USB_H)
+#if defined(HAVE_USB_H) || defined(HAVE_LUSB0_USB_H)
 /*
  * In order to make it easier for users, we try to figure out if a specific VID/PID is connected
  * to the computer. For that, going through the list of usb devices is more straightforward
-- 
